      6 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَدَانَوْا</span></b>  <i>They drew near,</i> or <i>approached, one
to another.</i> (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Hence,] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تدانى</span> <i>It</i> (a
thing) <i>drew together,</i> or <i>contracted;</i> or <i>became
drawn together</i> or <i>contracted.</i> (M* and L in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قلص</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَدَانَتْ إِبِلُ الرَّجُلَ</span> <i>The camels of
the man became few and weak.</i> (M.)

